# tools/s/shim_reason_witness.rish -- a guard hands on its target's reason, not only its verdict.
#
# THE LAW, IN ONE LINE. Whatever this tree runs on a reader's behalf, it carries that thing's own
# sentence back to the reader. Rishi's `run` files a target's stdout in `r.out` and its stderr in
# `r.err`, and only what a caller says reaches anyone. The exit code always travels. The sentence
# travels when somebody carries it.
#
# THREE SHAPES OF THE ONE LAW, each proven in its own pen below.
#   1  A pass-through SHIM above `tools/gen/` says `r.out`, exits `r.code`, and keeps the reason.
#   2  A witness over a CONTROL interpolates `${ctl.out}`, where the control names its failing
#      behavior on stderr so a passing run stays quiet.
#   3  A witness says the right thing one line too late -- `say scan.out` standing BELOW the assert
#      that fires, where `assert` stops the run and the say never happens.
#
# MEASURED ON A REAL FILE, `20260906`, WITH NO PLANT. `tools/am/amphora_device_wire.rish` drives a
# virtio lab and this pier holds no qemu, so it refuses honestly every time it runs. Run its target
# directly and a reader receives `rishi: assertion failed -- Amphora vessel fetch device wire lab
# failed`, line number beside it. Run the shim the same second and stderr holds zero bytes; the
# whole of what arrives is `amphora-device-wire: virtio fetch-by-digest lab...`, a progress line
# printed before the failure, which reads like success.
# `tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh` files a guard with `> out 2>&1`, so the merge stands
# ready and receives nothing: the shim emitted nothing to merge.
#
# AND THE THIRD SHAPE FIRED TWICE IN ONE MORNING, on the fleet's own metal. The cold pass of
# `20260907.042817` came back `guards_red=2`, and neither evidence page could name its cause.
# `index_row_bound` carried a real fault -- one row of the open day shelf standing above a newer
# one -- and named it the moment its scan ran by hand. `shipped_binary_claim` passed on the next
# run and on every run after, which is a flake, and a flake is diagnosable only from what it wrote
# down the first time. Both witnesses printed their target below the assert that fired.
#
# PROVEN ON METAL, `20260907`, with that morning's own refusal in a pen. A fixture printing
# `rows=16`, `rows_misordered=1`, `verdict=rows_misordered` and exiting 1, under a witness saying
# `scan.out` after the assert, produced two lines and both were the witness's own. The same fixture
# under the same witness with the say moved one line up produced all three readings, then the
# assertion. One line's position is the whole difference, and the repair is a move: say before you
# assert.
#
# EACH SHAPE KEEPS A GATE AND A RATCHET. The gate holds the rostered population at zero, since the
# fleet runs those files every lap and files their output as the evidence a hand reads. The ratchet
# carries the residue off the roster under a ceiling that only falls, so the tree improves on touch
# and each repair lands with its own number.
#
# THE GATES ARE PROVEN ABLE TO BITE, which matters more here than usual: each reads ZERO on this
# field, so the field alone could never show one working. The control supplies what the field
# withholds -- one plant per gate, refused by name, then one line moved or added and freed.
#
# THE ANCHOR. A seat is a `path` row standing alone at column zero, and a path named inside a
# roster comment stays prose. The control plants exactly that sentence in two of the three shapes,
# so a guard counts as rostered because the roster seats it rather than because somebody wrote
# about it.
#
# THE MATCHED FORMS STAY DISTINCT. A control may describe its shape; a witness may say some
# OTHER run's stderr, or some other run's stdout, and neither answers for the run under reading.
# Each shape's reading is bound to one variable's own spellings, and the control plants the
# confusable case beside the real one.
#
# THE CORPUS ARRIVES THROUGH `git grep`, whose status is classified rather than swallowed -- exit 1
# means no match, 2 or more means could not run, and one fallback reading both alike would report
# an empty answer as a clean tree (REDS %473, %484). Three greps over every tracked `.rish` cost 22
# seconds on this pier and the pre-filter reads the same counts in 2; the ordering reading walks
# every tracked `.rish` in ONE awk invocation keyed on `FILENAME`, 2,293 files in 0.2 seconds where
# a per-file loop cost 9. This guard stands at `tier lap`, so its own cost is somebody's morning.
#
# WHAT IT REACHES, and where it stops. The shim reading knows its subject by three marks together
# -- the `run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" ...]` call, the `say r.out` forward, and the `exit r.code`
# tail -- since each mark alone is ordinary. Two tracked files exit a captured run's code under
# another variable name and stand outside it; both are named every pass as `exit_alias_sites`, so
# the floor carries a number (REDS %466). The ordering reading counts by PATH, so a body reachable
# through a symlink is read twice and repaired once.
# Full-line comments are excluded from the shim and interpolation matches. Inline comments,
# quoted code, and conditional forwarding remain outside this text reading's proof.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/s/shim_reason_witness.rish

say "shim-reason: Language EN -- a shim is read for whether its target's refusal reaches a reader."
say "shim-reason: Style Gauge, Meter -- one gate at zero, one ratchet that only falls, the repair named in the refusal."
say "shim-reason: Lens TAME -- safety first: a guard that refuses without saying why costs the next reader the whole diagnosis."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/shim_reason_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
say scan.err
assert scan.ok else "shim-reason: the field reading refused -- read the scan's own lines above, which name every swallowing shim by path"
assert scan.out contains "swallow_rostered=0" else "shim-reason: a shim the standing roster names must forward `r.err`, since the fleet runs it and files its output as evidence"
assert scan.out contains "reason_lost_rostered=0" else "shim-reason: a rostered witness whose control names its failing behavior on stderr must interpolate that stderr, or its evidence page reads pass=N fail=1 and nothing a hand can act on"
assert scan.out contains "late_say_rostered=0" else "shim-reason: a rostered binding must print what its run wrote BEFORE the assert that judges it -- assert stops the run, so a say on the next line never happens when the target refuses"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "shim-reason: the scan must balance before it is believed"
say "field GREEN -- the matched shim, control and output-order forms meet their roster gates and residue ceilings"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/shim_reason_control.sh"]
say control.out
say control.err
assert control.ok else "shim-reason: the control must complete"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "shim-reason: the control must reach its own close"
assert control.out contains "clean_exit=0" else "shim-reason: a forwarding rostered shim must pass free, or every refusal below is the pen speaking"
assert control.out contains "clean_free=yes" else "shim-reason: a forwarding rostered shim must read verdict=ok"
assert control.out contains "clean_shim_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: the scan must name how many shims it found, or a reading of nothing looks like a healthy tree (REDS %463)"
assert control.out contains "clean_forward_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: a forwarding shim must be counted as forwarding, not merely left uncounted"
assert control.out contains "clean_gate_zero=yes" else "shim-reason: the gate must read zero on a clean pen, or its zero on the field means nothing"
assert control.out contains "rostered_exit=1" else "shim-reason: a rostered swallowing shim must exit non-zero"
assert control.out contains "rostered_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: a rostered shim that drops the reason must refuse -- this is the gate the field cannot supply"
assert control.out contains "rostered_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: the gate's refusal must carry a count, never only a verdict"
assert control.out contains "rostered_named=yes" else "shim-reason: the refusal must name the shim by path, since a count is not something a hand can open"
assert control.out contains "rostered_lifted=yes" else "shim-reason: adding the one forwarding line must free the same pen, or the refusal cannot be told from a scan that reds on everything"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_free_exit=0" else "shim-reason: the residue standing AT its ceiling must pass"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_free=yes" else "shim-reason: two unrostered swallowers at a ceiling of two must read ok"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: the ratchet must name its own count beside the ceiling"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_bitten_exit=1" else "shim-reason: the same plant one ceiling lower must exit non-zero"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: a ceiling proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass"
assert control.out contains "three_marks_needed=yes" else "shim-reason: a file carrying only two of the three marks is not a shim -- each mark alone is ordinary"
assert control.out contains "three_marks_corpus_read=yes" else "shim-reason: the near-misses must be read and rejected, rather than never reached"
assert control.out contains "three_marks_free=yes" else "shim-reason: a pen holding one forwarding shim and three near-misses must pass free"
assert control.out contains "untracked_unseen=yes" else "shim-reason: an untracked shim must not be counted -- the claim is about what the repository carries"
assert control.out contains "tracked_then_seen=yes" else "shim-reason: the same file once tracked must be counted, or the untracked reading is blindness rather than scope"
assert control.out contains "tracked_then_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: a newly tracked swallowing shim must land in the ratchet"
assert control.out contains "mention_not_a_seat=yes" else "shim-reason: a path named inside a roster comment is prose, not a seat"
assert control.out contains "mention_falls_to_ratchet=yes" else "shim-reason: a mentioned-but-unrostered swallower belongs to the ratchet, never the gate"
assert control.out contains "real_row_is_a_seat=yes" else "shim-reason: a genuine `path` row at column zero must be read as a seat, or the anchor has gone blind"
assert control.out contains "roster_refusal_exit=2" else "shim-reason: an unreadable roster must refuse at the instrument level"
assert control.out contains "roster_refusal=yes" else "shim-reason: without a roster every shim reads unrostered and the gate reports zero while measuring nothing"
assert control.out contains "roster_never_reads_ok=yes" else "shim-reason: a reading that could not tell rostered from unrostered must never answer ok"
assert control.out contains "roster_restored=yes" else "shim-reason: restoring the roster must return the pen's own refusal, so the refusal belongs to the roster's absence"
assert control.out contains "empty_corpus_exit=2" else "shim-reason: a corpus of nothing must refuse rather than answer clean"
assert control.out contains "empty_corpus_refused=yes" else "shim-reason: no tracked .rish means the corpus never arrived, which is not the same as no fault (REDS %463)"
assert control.out contains "no_shims_exit=2" else "shim-reason: .rish files with no shim among them must refuse"
assert control.out contains "no_shims_refused=yes" else "shim-reason: a reading that matched no shim proves nothing about shims"
assert control.out contains "no_shims_corpus_named=yes" else "shim-reason: that refusal must still name how many files it read"
assert control.out contains "no_repo_refused=yes" else "shim-reason: outside a git repository the reading has no corpus and must say so"
assert control.out contains "alias_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: a file exiting a run's code under another name is the reading's blind spot and must be counted"
assert control.out contains "alias_named=yes" else "shim-reason: the blind spot must be named by path, so a later reader can check it rather than rediscover it"
assert control.out contains "alias_excludes_r=yes" else "shim-reason: a file exiting `r.code` is inside the reading and must not be counted as its edge"
assert control.out contains "instrument_refusal_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: a git grep that could not run must refuse by name -- REDS %473, one guard over"
assert control.out contains "instrument_never_reads_ok=yes" else "shim-reason: a broken instrument must never read as a tree with no blind spot in it"
assert control.out contains "instrument_pen_innocent=yes" else "shim-reason: the same pen unmutated must read clean, so the refusal belongs to its plant"
assert control.out contains "reason_exit=1" else "shim-reason: a rostered witness dropping its control's reason must exit non-zero"
assert control.out contains "reason_population_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: the population of stderr-reporting controls must be counted, or a reading of zero looks like a tree with none"
assert control.out contains "reason_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: the second shape's gate must refuse -- this is the case the field cannot supply once it is repaired"
assert control.out contains "reason_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: that refusal must carry a count, never only a verdict"
assert control.out contains "reason_named=yes" else "shim-reason: the refusal must name the witness by path, since a count is not something a hand can open"
assert control.out contains "reason_lifted=yes" else "shim-reason: adding the one interpolation must free the same pen, or the refusal cannot be told from a scan that reds on everything"
assert control.out contains "reason_lifted_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: the lifted pen must read zero, so the count moves with the repair"
assert control.out contains "reason_ceiling_free_exit=0" else "shim-reason: the second residue standing AT its ceiling must pass"
assert control.out contains "reason_ceiling_free=yes" else "shim-reason: one unrostered loser at a ceiling of one must read ok"
assert control.out contains "reason_ceiling_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: the second ratchet must name its own count beside its ceiling"
assert control.out contains "reason_ceiling_bitten_exit=1" else "shim-reason: the same plant one ceiling lower must exit non-zero"
assert control.out contains "reason_ceiling_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: a ceiling proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass"
assert control.out contains "reason_stdout_unpopulated=yes" else "shim-reason: a control keeping its FAIL line on stdout is not in the population -- its reason already travels"
assert control.out contains "reason_stdout_free=yes" else "shim-reason: a witness over a stdout-reporting control is already correct and must pass free"
assert control.out contains "reason_other_var_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: forwarding some OTHER run's stderr must not credit the control's -- the blind reading is `mentions .err anywhere`"
assert control.out contains "reason_quoted_mention_unseen=yes" else "shim-reason: a control that only WRITES a stderr-reporting control is a mention, never an instance -- this reading counted itself once"
assert control.out contains "reason_quoted_mention_free=yes" else "shim-reason: a witness over such a control must pass free, since that control never writes to stderr at all"
assert control.out contains "reason_comment_unseen=yes" else "shim-reason: a control may DESCRIBE the shape in a comment without using it"
assert control.out contains "reason_comment_free=yes" else "shim-reason: a commented mention must leave the witness above it free"
assert control.out contains "reason_other_var_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: that case must be counted as a loss rather than merely left unfree"

assert control.out contains "order_free_exit=0" else "shim-reason: a witness saying its run before judging it must pass free"
assert control.out contains "order_free=yes" else "shim-reason: that pen must read verdict=ok, or every refusal below is the pen speaking"
assert control.out contains "order_free_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: and its count must read zero, or the zero on the field means nothing"
assert control.out contains "order_bitten_exit=1" else "shim-reason: the same two lines the other way round must exit non-zero"
assert control.out contains "order_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: a rostered binding printing its run below the assert must refuse -- this is the gate the field cannot supply once it is repaired"
assert control.out contains "order_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: that refusal must carry a count, never only a verdict"
assert control.out contains "order_named=yes" else "shim-reason: the refusal must name the binding by path and variable, since a count is not something a hand can open"
assert control.out contains "order_lifted=yes" else "shim-reason: moving the one line back must free the same pen, or the refusal cannot be told from a scan that reds on everything"
assert control.out contains "order_ceiling_free_exit=0" else "shim-reason: the third residue standing AT its ceiling must pass"
assert control.out contains "order_ceiling_free=yes" else "shim-reason: one unrostered late say at a ceiling of one must read ok"
assert control.out contains "order_ceiling_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: the third ratchet must name its own count beside its ceiling"
assert control.out contains "order_ceiling_bitten_exit=1" else "shim-reason: the same plant one ceiling lower must exit non-zero"
assert control.out contains "order_ceiling_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: a ceiling proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass"
assert control.out contains "order_silent_unseen=yes" else "shim-reason: a witness that never says its run has nothing standing in the wrong place -- that is a different fault and belongs to a different number"
assert control.out contains "order_silent_free=yes" else "shim-reason: and such a witness must pass this reading free"
assert control.out contains "order_err_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: a late `say r.err` loses exactly what a late `say r.out` loses"
assert control.out contains "order_other_var_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: a say belonging to a DIFFERENT run must not answer for this one -- the blind reading is `is there a say below an assert`"
assert control.out contains "order_other_var_named=yes" else "shim-reason: and the refusal must name which variable is late, since a file may hold both shapes at once"
assert control.out contains "order_mention_not_a_seat=yes" else "shim-reason: a path named inside a roster comment is prose in this shape too"
assert control.out contains "order_mention_falls_to_ratchet=yes" else "shim-reason: a mentioned-but-unrostered late say belongs to the ratchet, never the gate"

assert control.out contains "order_instrument_planted=yes" else "shim-reason: the parser fault must change the fixture before it is tested"
assert control.out contains "order_instrument_exit=2" else "shim-reason: a failed ordering parser must exit as an instrument refusal"
assert control.out contains "order_instrument_named=yes" else "shim-reason: the parser failure must name its instrument verdict"
assert control.out contains "order_instrument_count_withheld=yes" else "shim-reason: a failed parser has no ordering count to publish"
assert control.out contains "order_instrument_lifted=yes" else "shim-reason: the original parser must accept the same repository"

assert control.out contains "caller_absent_exit=0" else "shim-reason: a completed search with no callers must pass"
assert control.out contains "caller_absent_free=yes" else "shim-reason: exit 1 from git grep means no matches"
assert control.out contains "caller_2_exit=yes" else "shim-reason: a caller search error must exit 2"
assert control.out contains "caller_2_named=yes" else "shim-reason: the search failure must name instrument_refusal"
assert control.out contains "caller_2_count_withheld=yes" else "shim-reason: partial search output cannot support a population count"
assert control.out contains "caller_2_diagnostic=yes" else "shim-reason: the Git diagnostic must reach the reader"
assert control.out contains "caller_128_exit=yes" else "shim-reason: a caller search error must exit 2"
assert control.out contains "caller_128_named=yes" else "shim-reason: the search failure must name instrument_refusal"
assert control.out contains "caller_128_count_withheld=yes" else "shim-reason: partial search output cannot support a population count"
assert control.out contains "caller_128_diagnostic=yes" else "shim-reason: the Git diagnostic must reach the reader"
assert control.out contains "caller_restored_bitten=yes" else "shim-reason: the restored search must find the witness that drops stderr"
assert control.out contains "caller_repaired_free=yes" else "shim-reason: forwarding stderr must free the same repository"


# Full-line comment words do not establish a source match.
assert control.out contains "comment_shim_exit=1" else "shim-reason: a full-line comment cannot forward a shim result"
assert control.out contains "comment_shim_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: the swallowing shim must remain counted"
assert control.out contains "comment_shim_lifted_exit=0" else "shim-reason: real forwarding must free the same shim"
assert control.out contains "comment_shim_lifted=yes" else "shim-reason: the forwarding count must follow the repair"
assert control.out contains "comment_marks_exit=0" else "shim-reason: commented run and say forms must leave the real shim free"
assert control.out contains "comment_marks_unseen=yes" else "shim-reason: only the real shim supplies all three source marks"
assert control.out contains "comment_marks_restored_exit=1" else "shim-reason: restoring the source forms must expose both swallowers"
assert control.out contains "comment_marks_restored=yes" else "shim-reason: both restored shims must return to the population"
assert control.out contains "comment_reason_exit=1" else "shim-reason: a comment mentioning stderr cannot carry the control result"
assert control.out contains "comment_reason_counted=yes" else "shim-reason: the witness that loses stderr must remain counted"
assert control.out contains "comment_reason_lifted_exit=0" else "shim-reason: real interpolation must free the same witness"
assert control.out contains "comment_reason_lifted=yes" else "shim-reason: the loss count must fall with the repair"
assert control.out contains "comment_out_exit=0" else "shim-reason: a stdout mention in a comment is outside the interpolation population"
assert control.out contains "comment_out_unseen=yes" else "shim-reason: commented stdout must add no loss to this reading"

say "RED and GREEN paths proven -- the control's own `cases=` and `repos=` lines above carry the totals, and every refusal is lifted in its own pen"
say "GREEN: shim-reason -- the matched diagnostic forms pass, and the controls prove their refusals."
